{"id": "EUVD-2026-55286", "enisaUuid": "0bcb093d-3204-3f07-98b6-bf4102cf3154", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nLoongArch: Move jump_label_init() before parse_early_param()\n\nWhen enabling both CONFIG_MEM_ALLOC_PROFILING=y and\nCONFIG_MEM_ALLOC_PROFILING_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT=y, then diabling memory\nprofiling by adding the boot parameter 'sysctl.vm.mem_profiling=0' will\ncause the kernel failed to boot.\n\nAfter analysis, this is because jump_label_init() must be called before\nparse_early_param(), the early param handlers may modify static keys by\nstatic_branch_enable/disable().\n\nFix this by moving jump_label_init() to before parse_early_param(). The\nsolution is similar to other architectures.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T11:59:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:31", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1d0b99ef7fcb6cef1df273872059bf854814500e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4b40e590efb350c54480d7e883f054d3609a94c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/38b025fcdc45bdf5140a5726a1fbb2e694ea047b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/881e9f3c4e117b100880b1c5de3a0da8e455a78f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ea68d444a658783234a06f05414e41cf93a18fb2"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pcxf-938w-xxq5", "CVE-2026-68185"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3973ca83-d13b-3a4e-9264-c984a7f215e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}, {"id": "3b443aa5-b4c2-3b40-8348-758efe9423bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "628c3bb40e9a8cefc0a6fde28b7b66bfe46d1dc2 <1d0b99ef7fcb6cef1df273872059bf854814500e"}, {"id": "59c4a2e2-2bc0-376a-bd26-5de52f442621", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "690435ee-f2ba-3a30-b692-f154d63d1f0b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "628c3bb40e9a8